Problem: Remove Element (LC 27)

Pattern: Two Pointers

Approach:

1. Use two pointers: one pointer checks every element and the other keeps track of where the next valid element should go.
2. Start both pointers at the beginning.
3. Check each element using the fast pointer.
4. If the element is equal to the given value, ignore it.
5. If the element is not equal to the given value, place it at the position of the slow pointer.
6. Move the slow pointer forward after placing a valid element.
7. Move the fast pointer forward after checking each element.
8. When all elements are checked, the slow pointer represents the number of valid elements.
9. Return the number of valid elements.

Key Idea:
The fast pointer searches for valid elements, while the slow pointer collects them at the beginning of the array.

Time Complexity: O(n)

Space Complexity: O(1)
